{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Remediated the 5 blocking findings from the prior signed BLOCK plan-review:\n\n1. [E6/E1/F1 cache AC] Added an explicit cache-reuse AC — the live exhaustion run's successor usage log must show cache-read tokens > 0, proving the shared prefix hit the prompt cache.\n2. [G1G2 config naming] Renamed the three new keys to FLAT completion_* dataclass fields on VerifyConfig (completion_recovery_pool_multiplier=1.5, completion_verify_steps_per_criterion=8, completion_verify_step_floor_min=48), matching the existing completion_priority_floor/completion_floor_active convention at _config_schema.py:236/246. No dotted completion.* section is introduced. Verified no name collision.\n3. [T3 cache mechanism] Rewrote the Cache section to name the REAL mechanism: the automatic cache_settings_for arms (capabilities.py:679-701) — always-on cache_instructions+cache_tool_definitions plus the message-tail arm (anthropic_cache/bedrock_cache_messages) gated on execution_mode in _MESSAGE_TAIL_EXECUTION_MODES, breakpoint at prompt/message-tail END — NOT a hand-placed inline CachePoint. Dropped the CachePoint claim.\n4. [T8 model vocab] Replaced Sonnet-class/frontier-class with the real model_classes.py vocabulary trivial/standard/frontier; batch cap keys on the resolved class slot (standard=>8, frontier=>12, trivial=>8), resolved by matching the verifier model against the slot defaults (model_classes.py:47-56), unrecognized => standard cap 8.\n5. [T8 fallback consumer] Fixed the deterministic_fallback certification story: it sets certifiable=false on its OWN emitted verdict (the completion_sidecar.py:290 seam the signing path already reads), stamped finalizer=deterministic_fallback — distinct from child_closure_findings (which derives certifiable=false from CHILD signatures, completion.py:90-193).\n\nAlso addressed key advisories: added the _VERIFY_MIN_STEPS reference inventory (tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py updated in-change; operations.py:36 comment-only) and the _recover call-site note to Scope; added a record_criterion_verdict schema AC (met is bool-only, absence=unbanked) and a downgrade-authority AC; noted lever 1/2 epic-scope provenance (discovered via d2df, folded under operator approval). Re-running plan-review."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786070919302940001,"uuid":"7cec0bfb-e54f-47f3-b5b3-a53bd7594af1"}